=== King-attack curve, fitted against Stockfish's static evaluation instead of game results ===
Date        2026-08-30
Corpus      tuning-data/mychess-selfplay-960.epd, 39,619 positions, all usable
Target      Stockfish 18 static NNUE `eval`  minus  WeightingFunction.calculate, both white-POV,
            both static -- no search on either side. Clipped to +/-2000 cp.
Features    phase-scaled attack-unit indicator, identical to KingAttackTexelData.featuresOf
Estimator   ordinary least squares (ridge 1e-6), 200 block bootstrap replicates, block 8
Units       KingAttackUnits (P1 N2 B2 R3 Q5), 3x3 king zone, rays stop at the first piece

WHY. The outcome-labelled fit over this same corpus labels every position with the result of a
myChess SELF-PLAY game. If myChess is blind to king attacks then neither side converts one, so the
fit learns "attack units are worthless" from games that blindness produced. The positions are fine;
only the label is circular. Replacing the label with a far stronger, independent evaluator removes
that -- no game outcome enters at any point. Stockfish's NNUE is itself trained on games, so this
is not a first-principles ground truth; it is a yardstick myChess's own play cannot have moved.

PLACEBO. Bearing on the king zone also means having active pieces deep in enemy territory, and a
regression cannot separate the two on its own. The placebo column repeats the whole fit over a 3x3
zone on the king's rank, four files away -- same depth, same side of the board, no king. Whatever
the placebo also earns is activity rather than danger.

