READING IT. Indices 6-8 land at 44.2 / 45.6 / 85.5 against the shipped curve's 49 / 40 / 83 -- two
estimators with different labels agreeing at the top. That agreement is what makes the disagreement
at 3-5 credible: a systematically shifted estimator would have moved the top entries too. At index
5 the outcome-labelled fit gives -3.0 [-9.5, +12.0] and this one +15.2 [11.0, 19.4], with the
placebo at -8.6 [-12.3, -3.4] -- disjoint. Indices 1-2 remain indistinguishable from zero on both.

CONSEQUENCE. docs/king-safety.md 4.5 zeroes indices 1-5 on the strength of overlapping bootstrap
intervals from the outcome-labelled fits. On this evidence that zeroing is an artifact of the label
for indices 3, 4 and 5. It is NOT a repair on its own: +15 cp stands against a 475 cp gap in the
position that prompted the measurement (BlunderTest.staticEval960_afterDxc6, 5 units on the black
king, myChess -194 where Stockfish reads +281 statically).

Raw per-position data was not kept -- it is 39,619 lines of intermediate values and reproducible
from the corpus. The driver itself is not yet in tools/: it needs a batch probe and a
configurable-center variant of KingAttackUnits in test sources. Porting it is an open task.
